  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Auth0 tenant log event → AKSI control ID mapping. Auth0 (https://auth0.com/docs/api/management/v2/logs) is the second-most-used enterprise identity provider after Okta — particularly common for B2C and SaaS. The /api/v2/logs endpoint exports tenant events: logins, signups, consent grants, token exchanges, password changes, connection updates, and Management API operations. Mapping is type-code driven (Auth0 uses short codes like 's' for success-login, 'f' for failure, 'ublkd' for blocked-user) with overlays for scope-based privilege detection, federation strategy, mobile sessions, and cross-country actor patterns. Privileged scope grants (admin / read:users / update:users) raise a PR-02 FLAG. Cross-country pattern (one user_id touching > N distinct country_codes in an export) produces a synthetic PR-01 FLAG. PII redaction: ip masked to /16, user_agent truncated to first 80 + sha256, details.auth.user.email reduced to email-domain only, details.auth.user.name reduced to length + sha256, location_info reduced to country_code only (city / latitude / longitude dropped — too granular for evidence).",
